  "limitations": [
    "Trained on 80 real chips from three flood events (Assam 2016, Pakistan 2017, Sri Lanka 2017); tested on 29. This is a small-data flood-mapping model, not a nationally validated one.",
    "Maps where water IS in one radar image. It does not forecast floods, estimate depth, or tell flood water from a permanent river without a reference water layer.",
    "Radar confusions remain: wind-roughened water and flooded vegetation are missed; smooth dry surfaces, sand bars and radar shadow can be mistaken for water.",
    "No live Sentinel-1 feed is connected: it runs on the chips on disk or an uploaded GeoTIFF. Not connected to the risk engine or alerts.",
    "Scores on synthetic India chips measure agreement with a simulator, not accuracy over India."
  ]
